charge"],"needs_review":false,"review_note":null,"last_verified":"2026-11-03"},{"iso3":"EGY","name":"Egypt","region":"North","recs":["COMESA"],"capital":"Cairo","population_m":114.54,"ag_gdp_pct":13.7,"ag_jobs_pct":18.7,"electricity_access_pct":100,"internet_users_pct":74.6,"caadp_br4_score":6.83,"aidi_rank":2,"aidi_score":91.43,"deep":true,"summary":"Agriculture contributes about 13.7% of GDP and employs about 18.7% of workers, with a 4th CAADP Biennial Review score of 6.83/10 against the 9.29 benchmark (not on track). Around 100% of the population has electricity access and 74.6% use the internet, with an AfDB AIDI 2024 score of 91.43 (rank 2/54).","narrative":"Egypt is ahead on state-led scale: it is reclaiming desert land under a centrally run megaproject model (the New Delta, about 2.2 million feddans, roughly LE800bn / $15bn spent so far, inaugurated May 2026), and it has paired this with drainage-water reuse, silos, logistics corridors and a digital Farmer's Card used for fertilizer payments. Policy is consistent, because agriculture is framed as a national-security issue. The government says it is self-sufficient in rice, sugar, poultry, eggs and fresh milk, and it is targeting 50% wheat self-sufficiency. The weak points are structural. Agriculture is almost entirely irrigated, so it depends on a fixed Nile allocation. Old-lands holdings are tiny and fragmented. Public investment runs through military-linked bodies (the Future of Egypt Authority, the Armed Forces Engineering Authority and NSPO), which crowds out private and smallholder-led models and makes the data less transparent. Research capacity is deep (ARC, ASRT), but extension has eroded and agri-tech startups are still small. Donors (Italy's AgriTech4Egypt, CGIAR, EBRD) fill much of the innovation-finance gap. Overall, Egypt leads on irrigation, storage and land-expansion infrastructure, and lags on farmer-level productivity, inclusive finance and water-use efficiency in the old lands.","strengths":["Fully irrigated system, with very large state investment in land reclamation (New Delta, Toshka, Sinai) and drainage-water treatment (El Hammam, up to 7.5 million m3/day)","Policy consistency: the 2030 Sustainable Agricultural Development Strategy and a 5-pillar food-security strategy (2026)","Self-sufficiency claimed in rice, sugar, poultry, eggs and fresh milk (MoALR, April 2026)","Strong research base: Agricultural Research Centre (ARC) and ASRT, with about 14 new varieties expected to be registered in 2026","Digital farmer registry and Farmer's Card for subsidized fertilizer payments, targeted for nationwide rollout by 2026","Export-oriented horticulture with access to EU and Gulf markets"],"flagship_programs":["Sustainable Agricultural Development Strategy 2030","New Delta / Toshka land reclamation projects","Hayah Karima (Decent Life) rural initiative"],"atlas":{"indicators":{"account_pct":43.1,"ag_spend_pct_budget":2.2,"ag_va_per_worker_usd":8942,"caadp_br4":6.83,"cereal_yield_t_ha":7.36,"electricity_pct":100,"fertilizer_kg_ha":407.39,"internet_pct":74.6,"irrigated_pct_cropland":89.95},"n_pillars":5,"pillars":{"finance":40,"infrastructure":91,"inputs_water":100,"policy":48,"productivity":94},"score":75},"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_African_countries_by_population","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_GDP_sector_composition","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_sector_composition_of_the_labor_force","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_electrification_rate","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_number_of_Internet_users","https://eoai-africa.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/4th_CAADP_Biennial_Review_Report-COMPLETE.pdf","https://intelpoint.co/insights/seychelles-tops-africas-2024-infrastructure-index-with-a-near-perfect-score-of-99-77/","https://africa.com/top-10-news/africas-infrastructure-race-the-10-countries-leading-the-charge","https://english.ahram.org.eg/News/565382.aspx","ht