_pct":10.1,"ag_jobs_pct":29.6,"electricity_access_pct":100,"internet_users_pct":91.2,"caadp_br4_score":6.99,"aidi_rank":7,"aidi_score":null,"deep":true,"summary":"Agriculture contributes about 10.1% of GDP and employs about 29.6% of workers, with a 4th CAADP Biennial Review score of 6.99/10 against the 9.29 benchmark (not on track). Around 100% of the population has electricity access and 91.2% use the internet, with an AfDB AIDI 2024 rank of 7/54.","narrative":"Morocco is the continent's most commercially advanced agricultural economy. Two decades of continuous strategy (Plan Maroc Vert 2008-2020, then Generation Green 2020-2030) have brought 108bn dirhams of contracted investment since 2020 across 20 programme contracts. Drip irrigation has reached ~930,000 ha toward a 1m-ha target, and OCP's fertiliser, agronomy and digital advisory ecosystem (Al Moutmir, UM6P) is world class. Ports (Tanger Med), roads and a high-renewables power system support export horticulture to Europe. The binding constraint is water. Multi-year droughts depleted dam reserves (agricultural dams were 26% full in Jan 2025), and the state's answer is the 2020-2027 National Drinking Water and Irrigation Programme plus 1.7bn m3/yr of desalination by 2030. The Generation Green mid-term review (BCG, 2026) is looking at an uneven split: export agriculture has thrived, while rain-fed smallholders, livestock and the rural 'middle class' target still lag. Collective and fragmented land tenure (soulaliyate lands) holds back investment. A new government (PM Fatima Ezzahra El Mansouri, Oct 2026) moved the agriculture portfolio to Khalid Hatimy and renamed it to include 'Food Sovereignty', which signals a shift toward domestic food security.","strengths":["Long-term strategy continuity (Plan Maroc Vert to Generation Green) with contract-based delivery","~930,000 ha under drip irrigation with state subsidy (FDA)","OCP/UM6P ecosystem: fertiliser, soil mapping, agronomic advisory, R&D","World-class logistics (Tanger Med) and strong renewable energy build-out","Export-oriented horticulture with EU market access"],"flagship_programs":["Generation Green 2020-2030","National Water Supply and Irrigation Programme 2020-2027"],"atlas":{"indicators":{"account_pct":44.4,"ag_spend_pct_budget":3.8,"ag_va_per_worker_usd":3898,"caadp_br4":6.99,"cereal_yield_t_ha":1.24,"electricity_pct":100,"fertilizer_kg_ha":40.18,"internet_pct":91.2,"irrigated_pct_cropland":20.08},"n_pillars":5,"pillars":{"finance":43,"infrastructure":98,"inputs_water":84,"policy":56,"productivity":59},"score":68},"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_African_countries_by_population","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_GDP_sector_composition","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_sector_composition_of_the_labor_force","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_electrification_rate","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_number_of_Internet_users","https://eoai-africa.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/4th_CAADP_Biennial_Review_Report-COMPLETE.pdf","https://africa.com/top-10-news/africas-infrastructure-race-the-10-countries-leading-the-charge","https://www.moroccoworldnews.com/2026/10/342433/khalid-hatimys-journey-from-agribusiness-to-being-moroccos-agriculture-minister/","https://www.moroccoworldnews.com/2026/10/342414/king-mohammed-vi-presides-over-ceremony-to-appoint-new-government-members/","https://old.medias24.com/2026/04/21/to-accelerate-its-transformation-ocp-overhauls-its-internal-organization-and-reshapes-its-top-leadership-1663207/","https://africa24tv.com/morocco-108-billion-dirhams-invested-since-2020-to-transform-agriculture/","https://hortidaily.com/article/9639707/morocco-wants-to-equip-one-million-hectares-with-localized-irrigation-by-2030","https://www.moroccoworldnews.com/2025/07/228204/morocco-sets-sights-on-2030-water-security-with-boost-to-desalination-dam-projects/"],"needs_review":false,"review_note":null,"last_verified":"2026-11-03"