caadp_br4":5.09,"cereal_yield_t_ha":0.04,"electricity_pct":98.6,"fertilizer_kg_ha":3.28,"internet_pct":74.7,"irrigated_pct_cropland":6.48},"n_pillars":4,"pillars":{"finance":null,"infrastructure":88,"inputs_water":44,"policy":42,"productivity":40},"score":54},"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_African_countries_by_population","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_GDP_sector_composition","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_sector_composition_of_the_labor_force","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_electrification_rate","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_number_of_Internet_users","https://www.jica.go.jp/english/jica_ri/publication/knowledge/__icsFiles/afieldfile/2024/12/20/Knowledge_Report_No10.pdf","https://africa.com/top-10-news/africas-infrastructure-race-the-10-countries-leading-the-charge"],"needs_review":false,"review_note":null,"last_verified":"2026-11-03"},{"iso3":"CIV","name":"Cote d'Ivoire","region":"West","recs":["ECOWAS"],"capital":"Yamoussoukro","population_m":31.17,"ag_gdp_pct":17.9,"ag_jobs_pct":45.2,"electricity_access_pct":71.1,"internet_users_pct":41.4,"caadp_br4_score":3.96,"aidi_rank":null,"aidi_score":null,"deep":true,"summary":"Agriculture contributes about 17.9% of GDP and employs about 45.2% of workers, with a 4th CAADP Biennial Review score of 3.96/10 against the 9.29 benchmark (not on track). Around 71.1% of the population has electricity access and 41.4% use the internet, with no AIDI 2024 score captured here.","narrative":"Côte d'Ivoire is among West Africa's best performers. It is the world leader in cocoa, cashew and rubber. Agriculture provides about 17% of GDP, 40% of exports and 40% of jobs, and total output exceeded 37 million tonnes in 2025, with food crops up 9% to 25.8 million tonnes. The main driver is policy consistency. Two successive National Agricultural Investment Programmes ran under the same leadership: PNIA 1 (2012-2017, ~2,040bn FCFA) and PNIA 2 (2018-2025, ~12,391bn FCFA). PNIA 3 was launched in June 2026 under the 2026-2030 National Development Plan, with axes on food sovereignty, competitiveness, financing, rural land security and climate resilience. The Conseil du Café-Cacao has stabilized farm-gate prices (at least 60% of the CIF price). Local processing has reached roughly 41% for cocoa and 43% for cashew, supported by good ports (Abidjan, San-Pédro), relatively reliable power and the AfDB headquarters in Abidjan. The country is held back by rural land insecurity (only about 2 million ha certified as of late 2026), low irrigation and mechanization in food crops (rice still largely imported), thin agricultural credit, and ageing cocoa orchards under swollen-shoot disease and deforestation scrutiny (EUDR). The government changed in January 2026, when Bruno Koné replaced Kobenan Adjoumani, but it has signalled continuity.","strengths":["Policy continuity over three PNIA generations, with large investment envelopes","Global leadership in cocoa, cashew and rubber, and rising local processing (cocoa ~41%, cashew ~43%)","Strong logistics and power by regional standards (Abidjan and San-Pédro ports, relatively reliable grid)","Producer-financed research and extension model (FIRCA, CNRA, ANADER) and a new 2026-2035 research strategy","Active digital and agritech push (Orange, EU and GIZ DigiGreen & Agri fund; Yello Startup agritech prizes)"],"flagship_programs":["PNIA 2 (Programme National d'Investissement Agricole 2018-2025)","Agropoles programme"],"atlas":{"indicators":{"account_pct":57.6,"ag_spend_pct_budget":1.1,"ag_va_per_worker_usd":2368,"caadp_br4":3.96,"cereal_yield_t_ha":2.54,"electricity_pct":71.1,"fertilizer_kg_ha":14.71,"internet_pct":41.4,"irrigated_pct_cropland":0.51},"n_pillars":5,"pillars":{"finance":68,"infrastructure":62,"inputs_water":34,"policy":27,"productivity":74},"score":53},"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_African_countries_by_population","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_GDP_sector_composition","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_sector_composition_of_the_labor_force","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_electrification_rate","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_number_of_Internet_users","https://www.jica.go.jp/english/jica_ri/publication/knowledge/__icsFiles/afieldfile/2024/12/20/Knowledge_Report_No10.pdf","https://fr.allafrica.com/stories/202601290583.html","https://connectionivoirienne.net/2026/01/23/cote-divoire-le-gouvernement-mambe-ii-marque-par-la-sortie-dadjoumani/","https://www.aip.ci/cote-divoire-aip-le-ministre-bruno-kone-dresse-le-bilan-2025-du-secteur-agricole-et-annonce-les-perspectives-du-pnia-iii/","https://www.alwihdainfo.com/cote-divoire-bilan-agricole-2025-et-perspectives-du-pnia-iii/","https://connectionivoirienne.net/2026/06/19/economie-le-pm-mambe-lance-le-processus-dinvestissement-agricole-de-3eme-generation-pnia-3/","https://www.fratmat.info/article/2644229/economie/10e-edition-des-journees-nationales-du-cacao-et-du-chocolat-la-jeunesse-appelee-a-prendre-le-relais-pour-assurer-lavenir-de-la-filiere","https://www.fratmat.info/article/2645025/economie/securisation-fonciere-2-millions-dhectares-certifies","https://launchbaseafrica.com/orange-the-eu-and-giz-launch-8m-funding-initiative-to-back-agritech-startups-in-cote-divoire/?amp=1","https://launchbaseafrica.com/2024/10/22/gates-foundation-backs-ivorian-agritech-startup-grainotech"],"needs_review":false,"review_note":null,"last_verified":"2026-11-03"},{"iso3":"GMB","name":"Gambia","region":"West","recs":["ECOWAS"],"capital":"Banjul","population_m":2.7,"ag_gdp_pct":24.1,"ag_jobs_pct":29.1,"electricity_access_pct":63.7,"internet_users_pct":49.5,"caadp_br4_score":5.79,"aidi_rank":null,"aidi_score":null,"deep":false,"summary":"Agriculture contributes about 24.1% of GDP and employs about 29.1% of workers, with a 4th CAADP Biennial Review score of 5.79/10 against the 9.29 benchmark (not on track). Around 63.7% of the population has electricity access and 49.5% use the internet, with no AIDI 2024 score captured here.","narrative":null,"strengths":[],"flagship_programs":["Gambia National Agricultural Investment Plan (GNAIP II)"],"atlas":{"indicators":{"account_pct":38.2,"ag_spend_pct_budget":2.2,"ag_va_per_worker_usd":2218,"caadp_br4":5.79,"cereal_yield_t_ha":1,"electricity_pct":63.7,"fertilizer_kg_ha":15.33,"internet_pct":49.5,"irrigated_pct_cropland":1.12},"n_pillars":5,"pillars":{"finance":30,"infrastructure":61,"inputs_water":44,"policy":42,"productivity":42},"score":44},"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_African_countries_by_population","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_GDP_sector_composition","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_sector_composition_of_the_labor_force","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_electrification_rate","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_number_of_Internet_users","https://www.jica.go.jp/english/jica_ri/publication/knowledge/__icsFiles/afieldfile/2024/12/20/Knowledge_Report_No10.pdf"],"needs_review":false,"review_note":null,"last_verified":"2026-11-03"},{"iso3":"GHA","name":"Ghana","region":"West","recs":["ECOWAS"],"capital":"Accra","population_m":33.79,"ag_gdp_pct":20.7,"ag_jobs_pct":35.4,"electricity_access_pct":89.5,"internet_users_pct":72.2,"caadp_br4_score":6.68,"aidi_rank":null,"aidi_score":null,"deep":true,"summary":"Agriculture contributes about 20.7% of GDP and employs about 35.4% of workers, with a 4th CAADP Biennial Review score of 6.68/10 against the 9.29 benchmark (not on track). Around 89.5% of the population has electricity access and 72.2% use the internet, with no AIDI 2024 score captured here.","narrative":"Ghana sits in the middle of the pack. It has a vibrant agri-tech ecosystem (Farmerline, Complete Farmer) and high mobile-money penetration, but public agriculture policy resets with each change of government. Planting for Food and Jobs (2017-2024) gave way to the Feed Ghana Programme in 2025 under Minister Eric Opoku. Feed Ghana has focused on irrigation rehabilitation, small dams, solar boreholes, rice seed and Farmer Service Centres. Food inflation fell from 28.3% in January 2025 to 9.5% in October 2025, although macro stabilization contributed. Execution is constrained by fiscal stress. In 2026 the finance and agriculture ministries publicly disputed releases: MoFA said its H1 allotment was capped at GH¢910m, with only GH¢4.5m for the Feed Ghana line itself. Public agricultural spending remains well below the Malabo 10% target. Irrigation is minimal, with roughly 210,000 ha developed against about 1.9 million ha of potential, and existing schemes are often vandalized or left incomplete. COCOBOD's debt crisis and stranded beans weigh on the flagship export chain, and the 2026 reforms push toward local processing. Ghana is ahead of most peers on digital rails and on investor appetite for agritech, and behind on irrigation, mechanization and stable public finance.","strengths":["Dynamic agritech scene (Farmerline, Complete Farmer) with access to DFI and VC capital (IFC, Oikocredit, EU AgriFI)","High mobile-money penetration and digital farmer-profiling platforms","Feed Ghana Programme (2025) reprioritizing irrigation, seed systems, Farmer Service Centres and the poultry programme (Nkoko Nkitinkiti)","Food inflation fell to 9.5% by October 2025","MiDA, the GIDA board and ADB are aligned behind brownfield irrigation and agro-processing"],"flagship_programs":["Planting for Food and Jobs (PFJ 2.0)","Feed Ghana Programme"],"atlas":{"indicators":{"account_pct":81.2,"ag_spend_pct_budget":0.4,"ag_va_per_worker_usd":3747,"caadp_br4":6.68,"cereal_yield_t_ha":2.63,"electricity_pct":89.5,"fertilizer_kg_ha":18.35,"internet_pct":72.2,"irrigated_pct_cropland":2.83},"n_pillars":5,"pillars":{"finance":96,"infrastructure":80,"inputs_water":57,"policy":38,"productivity":80},"score":70},"sources":["https://en.wikipedi