.","narrative":null,"strengths":[],"flagship_programs":["Integrated soil and water conservation (dam) programme"],"atlas":{"indicators":{"account_pct":null,"ag_spend_pct_budget":null,"ag_va_per_worker_usd":null,"caadp_br4":null,"cereal_yield_t_ha":0.64,"electricity_pct":52.5,"fertilizer_kg_ha":1.87,"internet_pct":14.3,"irrigated_pct_cropland":3.03},"n_pillars":3,"pillars":{"finance":null,"infrastructure":28,"inputs_water":30,"policy":null,"productivity":12},"score":null},"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_African_countries_by_population","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_GDP_sector_composition","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_sector_composition_of_the_labor_force","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_electrification_rate","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_number_of_Internet_users","https://eoai-africa.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/4th_CAADP_Biennial_Review_Report-COMPLETE.pdf"],"needs_review":false,"review_note":null,"last_verified":"2026-11-03"},{"iso3":"ETH","name":"Ethiopia","region":"East","recs":["COMESA","IGAD"],"capital":"Addis Ababa","population_m":128.69,"ag_gdp_pct":34.9,"ag_jobs_pct":62.4,"electricity_access_pct":54.2,"internet_users_pct":21.4,"caadp_br4_score":null,"aidi_rank":null,"aidi_score":13.09,"deep":true,"summary":"Agriculture contributes about 34.9% of GDP and employs about 62.4% of workers, with a 4th CAADP Biennial Review score not captured in this dataset. Around 54.2% of the population has electricity access and 21.4% use the internet, with an AfDB AIDI 2024 score of 13.09.","narrative":"Ethiopia stands out for steady, state-led agricultural policy and long-term public spending. Agriculture averaged about 10.3% of public expenditure over 2009-2021, one of few African countries near the CAADP/Malabo target, although the share has slipped below 10% in recent years (FAO MAFAP). The Agricultural Transformation Institute (ATI) has driven cluster farming, which reached about 12.3m ha in 2024/25, and a large lowland irrigated-wheat push for import substitution. A 2025-2032 Digital Agriculture Roadmap is now in place. Second-level land certification (30m+ plots) and the 2024 Rural Land Proclamation allow use-rights to be leased and pledged as collateral. Even so, the state still owns all land, and FX shortages and high inflation limit fertiliser and machinery imports. Conflict in Amhara and Oromia, and before that Tigray, hurts production. Digital, power distribution and logistics infrastructure is weak, and Ethiopia is landlocked and depends on the Djibouti corridor. A new cabinet sworn in after the 2026 elections kept Addisu Arega at Agriculture, which signals continuity.","strengths":["Long-run public investment in agriculture near the CAADP 10% benchmark (avg 10.3% 2009-2021)","Dedicated delivery unit (ATI) with cluster farming covering ~12.3m ha and a Digital Agriculture Roadmap 2025-2032","Large-scale land certification (30m+ plots) enabling use-right collateral","Large hydropower base (incl. GERD) offering low-cost electricity potential for irrigation and agro-processing","Dense public extension network (development agents) and active irrigated-wheat import-substitution programme"],"flagship_programs":["Ten-Year Development Plan (2021-2030)","Grand Ethiopian Renaissance Dam (GERD)","Lowland irrigated wheat initiative"],"atlas":{"indicators":{"account_pct":48.8,"ag_spend_pct_budget":3.1,"ag_va_per_worker_usd":1154,"caadp_br4":null,"cereal_yield_t_ha":2.63,"electricity_pct":54.2,"fertilizer_kg_ha":40.27,"internet_pct":21.4,"irrigated_pct_cropland":0.98},"n_pillars":5,"pillars":{"finance":47,"infrastructure":37,"inputs_water":57,"policy":31,"productivity":62},"score":47},"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_African_countries_by_population","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_GDP_sector_composition","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_sector_composition_of_the_labor_force","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_electrification_rate","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_number_of_Internet_users","https://intelpoint.co/?p=4720","https://capitalethiopia.com/2026/10/08/pm-abiy-forms-new-cabinet-with-39-womens-representation/","https://addisfortune.news/breaking-news/prime-minister-abiy-reshuffles-agriculture-portfolio-taps-party-insider-as-minister","https://www.ena.et/web/eng/w/eng_8580001","https://fao.org/in-action/mafap/where-we-work/ethiopia/3/en","https://capitalethiopia.com/2025/02/10/ethiopia-bets-big-on-digital-agriculture-to-boost-food-security-with-2025-2032-roadmap","https://leap.unep.org/en/countries/et/national-legislation/rural-land-administration-and-use-proclamation-no-13242024","https://www.thereporterethiopia.com/38266/","https://www.capitalethiopia.com/2022/08/19/contract-farming-bill-passed/"],"needs_review":false,"review_note":null,"last_verified":"2026-11-03"},{"iso3":"KEN","name":"Kenya","region":"East","recs":["COMESA","EAC","IGAD"],"capital":"Nairobi","population_m":55.34,"ag_gdp_pct":21.3,"ag_jobs_pct":32.3,"electricity_access_pct":76.2,"internet_users_pct":35,"caadp_br4_score":6.28,"aidi_rank":null,"aidi_score":null,"deep":true,"summary":"Agriculture contributes about 21.3% of GDP and employs about 32.3% of workers, with a 4th CAADP Biennial Review score of 6.28/10 against the 9.29 benchmark (not on track). Around 76.2% of the population has electricity access and 35% use the internet, with no AIDI 2024 score captured here.","narrative":"Kenya leads East Africa on agri-tech because mobile money (M-Pesa) gives it a dense digital rail that startups such as Pula, Apollo Agriculture and One Acre Fund-style input-credit models build on. Strong research institutions (KALRO, ILRI, CIFOR-ICRAF, AGRA HQ) and a deep impact-investor ecosystem in Nairobi add to this. Policy direction has been relatively steady since the 2019 ASTGS, and the state now runs a digital farmer registry (KIAMIS, about 7 million farmers) to target subsidised fertiliser. Public money is the weak spot: the agriculture ministry got about Ksh75.5bn (~2.7% of the national budget) in FY2026/27 planning, and the wider sector sits near 3%, far below the CAADP/Malabo 10% target. Irrigation is also thin, with about 664,000 irrigated acres (2021/22 baseline) against a 1.29m-acre target for 2027/28. Devolution split extension and some agriculture functions to 47 counties, and an ageing extension workforce leaves a real gap between digital ambition and on-farm advice.","strengths":["Mobile-money and agri-fintech ecosystem (M-Pesa rails; insurtech such as Pula with 20m+ farmers insured across markets)","Regional hub for CGIAR and agri-development HQs (ILRI, CIFOR-ICRAF, AGRA) plus KALRO's national research network","Digital farmer registry (KIAMIS) used to target e-subsidy fertiliser, with about 7m farmers registered","Mostly renewable grid (geothermal and hydro) and relatively strong rural connectivity compared with peers","Export horticulture, tea and dairy value chains with established cold-chain and air-freight links"],"flagship_programs":["Agricultural Sector Transformation and Growth Strategy (ASTGS 2019-2029)","Bottom-Up Economic Transformation Agenda (BETA)"],"atlas":{"indicators":{"account_pct":90.1,"ag_spend_pct_budget":2.6,"ag_va_per_worker_usd":1633,"caadp_br4":6.28,"cereal_yield_t_ha":1.69,"electricity_pct":76.2,"fertilizer_kg_ha":44.81,"internet_pct":35,"irrigated_pct_cropland":3.6},"n_pillars":5,"pillars":{"finance":100,"infrastructure":58,"inputs_water":72,"policy":47,"productivity":57},"score":67},"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_African_countries_by_population","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_GDP_sector_composition","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_sector_composition_of_the_labor_force","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_electrification_rate","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_number_of_Internet_users","https://www.jica.go.jp/english/jica_ri/publication/knowledge/__icsFiles/afieldfile/2024/12/20/Knowledge_Report_No10.pdf","https://citizen.digital/article/cs-kagwe-pushes-for-more-budget-allocation-in-agriculture-sector-to-safeguard-food-security-n377722","https://citizen.digital/article/kenya-targets-doubling-irrigated-land-to-boost-food-security-by-2028-n383910","https://dairybusinessmea.com/2026/01/30/kalro-names-patrick-ketiem-as-director-general-after-kiregers-exit/","https://ag.purdue.edu/events/department/ansc/2026/10/better-lives-better-planet-through-livestock-science-partnerships-and-ilris-vision-to-2030.html","https://agra.org/agra-appoints-alice-ruhweza-as-next-president/","https://www.pula-advisors.com/about/","https://www.the-star.co.ke/counties/central/2026-01-15-government-rolls-out-125-million-subsidised-fertiliser-bags-ahead-of-long-rains","https://fsd.kilimo.go.ke/pdfs/agricultural-sector-transformation-and-growth-strategy.pdf","https://allafrica.com/stories/202601260517.html"],"needs_review":false,"review_note":null,"last_verified":"2026-11-03"},{"iso3":"MDG","name":"Madagascar","region":"East","recs":["COMESA","SADC"],"capital":"Antananarivo","population_m":31.2,"ag_gdp_pct":22.5,"ag_jobs_pct":69.4,"electricity_access_pct":35.1,"internet_users_pct":18.7,"caadp_br4_score":null,"aidi_rank":null,"aidi_score":13.43,"deep":false,"summary":"Agriculture contributes about 22.5% of GDP and employs about 69.4% of workers, with a 4th CAADP Biennial Review score not captured in this dataset. Around 35.1% of the population has electricity access and 18.7% use the internet, with an AfDB AIDI 2024 score of 13.43.","narrative":null,"strengths":[],"flagship_programs":["Plan Emergence Madagascar"],"atlas":{"indicators":{"account_pct":24.5,"ag_spend_pct_budget":4.5,"ag_va_per_worker_usd":306,"caadp_br4":null,"cereal_yield_t_ha":2.39,"electricity_pct":35.1,"fertilizer_kg_ha":6.06,"internet_pct":18.7,"irrigated_pct_cropland":30.17},"n_pillars":5,"pillars":{"finance":15,"infrastructure":18,"inputs_water":60,"policy":45,"productivity":47},"score":37},"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_African_countries_by_population","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_GDP_sector_composition","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_sector_composition_of_the_labor_force","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_electrification_rate","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_number_of_Internet_users","https://intelpoint.co/?p=4720"],"needs_review":false,"review_note":null,"last_verified":"2026-11-03"},{"iso3":"MUS","name":"Mauritius","region":"East","recs":["COMESA","SADC"],"capital":"Port Louis","population_m":1.27,"ag_gdp_pct":4.3,"ag_jobs_pct":5.3,"electricity_access_pct":100,"internet_users_pct":73.3,"caadp_br4_score":null,"aidi_rank":4,"aidi_score":82.77,"deep":false,"summary":"Agriculture contributes about 4.3% of GDP and employs about 5.3% of workers, with a 4th CAADP Biennial Review score not captured in this dataset. Around 100% of the population has electricity access and 73.3% use the internet, with an AfDB AIDI 2024 score of 82.77 (rank 4/54).","narrative":null,"strengths":[],"flagship_programs":["Food and agricultural sector strategy (food security fund)"],"atlas":{"indicators":{"account_pct":89.6,"ag_spend_pct_budget":1.7,"ag_va_per_worker_usd":20796,"caadp_br4":null,"cereal_yield_t_ha":11.89,"electricity_pct":100,"fertilizer_kg_ha":96.09,"internet_pct":73.3,"irrigated_pct_cropland":20.01},"n_pillars":5,"pillars":{"finance":98,"infrastructure":90,"inputs_water":92,"policy":17,"productivity":98},"score":79},"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_African_countries_by_population","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_GDP_sector_composition","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_sector_composition_of_the_labor_force","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_electrification_rate","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_number_of_Internet_users","https://intelpoint.co/insights/seychelles-tops-africas-2024-infrastructure-index-with-a-near-perfect-score-of-99-77/","https://africa.com/top-10-news/africas-infrastructure-race-the-10-countries-leading-the-charge"],"needs_review":false,"review_note":null,"last_verified":"2026-11-03"},{"iso3":"RWA","name":"Rwanda","region":"East","recs":["COMESA","EAC","ECCAS"],"capital":"Kigali","population_m":13.95,"ag_gdp_pct":24.6,"ag_jobs_pct":54.8,"electricity_access_pct":48.7,"internet_users_pct":31.7,"caadp_br4_score":8.07,"aidi_rank":null,"aidi_score":null,"deep":true,"summary":"Agriculture contributes about 24.6% of GDP and employs about 54.8% of workers, with a 4th CAADP Biennial Review score of 8.07/10 against the 9.29 benchmark (not on track). Around 48.7% of the population has electricity access and 31.7% use the internet, with no AIDI 2024 score captured here.","narrative":"Rwanda punches above its weight because policy is unusually consistent and well executed. It has run five successive Strategic Plans for Agriculture Transformation, and the current PSTA5 (2024-2029, ~US$5.1bn, 44% expected from the private sector) aligns with NST2 and has strong monitoring. It also has digital government and land registration that covers almost the whole country. Agricultural exports passed US$1bn for the first time in FY2025/26 on the back of NAEB's coffee, tea and horticulture work. The 2026/27 budget raised MINAGRI's allocation by 41%, which made it the biggest gainer, but agriculture's share of the total is still well under the Malabo 10%. Physical limits are hard: land is very scarce and hilly with tiny plots, and only ~75,000 ha (15% of irrigable land) is irrigated, with a target of 133k ha by 2029. Logistics are landlocked and costly, and agriculture gets only ~6% of commercial lending. Ministerial turnover in MINAGRI has been frequent (most recently Dec 2025), though technocratic continuity has softened its effect.","strengths":["Consistent, results-monitored strategy cycle (PSTA1-5) aligned with NST2","Agricultural exports surpassed US$1.1bn in FY2025/26 (coffee, tea, horticulture)","Near-universal land registration and strong digital-government rails (Irembo, mobile money)","Concessional ag-lending scheme halving rates (RWF 55bn approved, 30.9bn disbursed via 31 institutions)","Kigali as a regional innovation and convening hub (AGRF, investor-friendly RDB)"],"flagship_programs":["PSTA 5 (Strategic Plan for Agriculture Transformation 2024/25-2028/29)","Crop Intensification Programme"],"atlas":{"indicators":{"account_pct":42.1,"ag_spend_pct_budget":2.2,"ag_va_per_worker_usd":1615,"caadp_br4":8.07,"cereal_yield_t_ha":1.78,"electricity_pct":48.7,"fertilizer_kg_ha":24.64,"internet_pct":31.7,"irrigated_pct_cropland":5.01},"n_pillars":5,"pillars":{"finance":38,"infrastructure":35,"inputs_water":68,"policy":54,"productivity":59},"score":51},"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_African_countries_by_population","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_GDP_sector_composition","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_sector_composition_of_the_labor_force","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_electrification_rate","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_number_of_Internet_users","https://eoai-africa.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/4th_CAADP_Biennial_Review_Report-COMPLETE.pdf","https://www.minagri.gov.rw/updates/news-details/rwanda-launches-5th-strategic-plan-for-agriculture-transformation","https://www.minagri.gov.rw/updates/news-details/rwanda-agricultural-show-2026-stakeholders-urged-to-leverage-innovation-and-strategic-partnerships-for-agri-food-systems-transformation","https://allafrica.com/stories/202512020109.html","https://www.cia.gov/resources/world-leaders/historical-data/2026-july/rwanda/","https://allafrica.com/stories/202602030013.html","https://www.ktpress.rw/2026/07/rwandas-2026-27-budget-agriculture-biggest-winner-disaster-mana