0.4% of GDP and employs about 59.2% of workers, with a 4th CAADP Biennial Review score of 3.51/10 against the 9.29 benchmark (not on track). Around 7.1% of the population has electricity access and 6.67% use the internet, with an AfDB AIDI 2024 score of 7.38.","narrative":null,"strengths":[],"flagship_programs":["Comprehensive Agriculture Master Plan (CAMP)"],"atlas":{"indicators":{"account_pct":5.8,"ag_spend_pct_budget":27.2,"ag_va_per_worker_usd":null,"caadp_br4":3.51,"cereal_yield_t_ha":0.94,"electricity_pct":7.1,"fertilizer_kg_ha":0.18,"internet_pct":6.67,"irrigated_pct_cropland":3.88},"n_pillars":5,"pillars":{"finance":0,"infrastructure":0,"inputs_water":32,"policy":69,"productivity":27},"score":26},"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_African_countries_by_population","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_GDP_sector_composition","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_sector_composition_of_the_labor_force","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_electrification_rate","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_number_of_Internet_users","https://www.jica.go.jp/english/jica_ri/publication/knowledge/__icsFiles/afieldfile/2024/12/20/Knowledge_Report_No10.pdf","https://intelpoint.co/?p=4720"],"needs_review":false,"review_note":null,"last_verified":"2026-11-03"},{"iso3":"SDN","name":"Sudan","region":"East","recs":["COMESA","IGAD"],"capital":"Khartoum","population_m":50.04,"ag_gdp_pct":22.1,"ag_jobs_pct":null,"electricity_access_pct":61.8,"internet_users_pct":18.6,"caadp_br4_score":null,"aidi_rank":null,"aidi_score":null,"deep":false,"summary":"Agriculture contributes about 22.1% of GDP and employs about n/a of workers, with no score in the 4th CAADP Biennial Review (did not report in 2023). Around 61.8% of the population has electricity access and 18.6% use the internet, with no AIDI 2024 score captured here.","narrative":null,"strengths":[],"flagship_programs":["Gezira irrigation scheme"],"atlas":{"indicators":{"account_pct":15.3,"ag_spend_pct_budget":2.9,"ag_va_per_worker_usd":4706,"caadp_br4":null,"cereal_yield_t_ha":0.58,"electricity_pct":61.8,"fertilizer_kg_ha":7.03,"internet_pct":18.6,"irrigated_pct_cropland":7.39},"n_pillars":5,"pillars":{"finance":11,"infrastructure":35,"inputs_water":52,"policy":29,"productivity":42},"score":34},"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_African_countries_by_population","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_GDP_sector_composition","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_sector_composition_of_the_labor_force","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_electrification_rate","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_number_of_Internet_users","https://eoai-africa.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/4th_CAADP_Biennial_Review_Report-COMPLETE.pdf"],"needs_review":false,"review_note":null,"last_verified":"2026-11-03"},{"iso3":"TZA","name":"Tanzania","region":"East","recs":["EAC","SADC"],"capital":"Dodoma","population_m":66.62,"ag_gdp_pct":23.4,"ag_jobs_pct":65.4,"electricity_access_pct":42.7,"internet_users_pct":31.2,"caadp_br4_score":5.76,"aidi_rank":null,"aidi_score":null,"deep":true,"summary":"Agriculture contributes about 23.4% of GDP and employs about 65.4% of workers, with a 4th CAADP Biennial Review score of 5.76/10 against the 9.29 benchmark (not on track). Around 42.7% of the population has electricity access and 31.2% use the internet, with no AIDI 2024 score captured here.","narrative":"Tanzania is on an upward trajectory driven by a clear political mandate. Under Agenda 10/30, launched in 2022, the agriculture budget roughly tripled (TZS 294bn in 2021/22 to 954bn in 2022/23, then about TZS 1.1 trillion for 2026/27), and the irrigation budget rose more than sevenfold. Agenda 10/30 targets more than 10% sector growth, 8.5 million irrigated hectares and agro-processing raised from 10% to 50% by 2030. Outputs are rising. The country reports 130% food self-sufficiency, 23.8 million tonnes of food crops (2024/25) and 1.6 million tonnes of cash crops, and agriculture grew 4.0% in 2025, still well below the 10% target. Delivery leans on state programmes: NIRC borehole and scheme drilling, BBT youth block farms, and subsidized fertilizer and seed. A new National Agricultural Extension Services Agency (NAESA) starts in July 2026. The sector remains behind on irrigated area relative to its huge potential, mechanization, cold chain, rural power, and private finance and insurance. Even after the increases, the ministry vote is still only a few percent of the national budget, short of the Malabo 10% target. Cabinet continuity after the 2025 election (Minister Daniel Chongolo replaced Hussein Bashe) has so far preserved the agenda.","strengths":["Strong political commitment and budget growth under Agenda 10/30 (sector budget ~TZS 1.1tn in 2026/27)","Large land and water resources, food self-sufficiency (~130%) and a role as a regional food exporter","Rapid irrigation push: NIRC schemes, dams and a 67,000-borehole smallholder programme","Growing horticulture and avocado exports, and the SAGCOT corridor investment framework","High mobile-money penetration (M-Pesa, Tigo Pesa/Mixx, Airtel) enabling digital agri-services (MazaoHub, Kilimo Fresh)"],"flagship_programs":["Agenda 10/30","Building a Better Tomorrow (BBT) youth agribusiness","Agricultural Sector Development Programme II (ASDP II)"],"atlas":{"indicators":{"account_pct":59.8,"ag_spend_pct_budget":7.7,"ag_va_per_worker_usd":855,"caadp_br4":5.76,"cereal_yield_t_ha":1.87,"electricity_pct":42.7,"fertilizer_kg_ha":18.01,"internet_pct":31.2,"irrigated_pct_cropland":1.19},"n_pillars":5,"pillars":{"finance":70,"infrastructure":29,"inputs_water":48,"policy":70,"productivity":50},"score":53},"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_African_countries_by_population","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_GDP_sector_composition","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_sector_com